    rdfs:comment "Sam Hammond is a senior economist and policy analyst specialising in the intersection of transformative technology and governance, known for work at the Foundation for American Innovation. His analysis explores AI-driven economic disruption, techno-feudalism, the co-evolution of state institutions with autonomous systems, and the geopolitical implications of superintelligence, offering a libertarian-leaning but empirically grounded perspective on long-horizon AI futures."@en ;
