ngm:fair-adjudication a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Fair Adjudication"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Fair adjudication is the principle and process by which disputes are decided impartially, with due process, transparent rules, and the absence of bias toward any party. In legal and decentralised-arbitration contexts it requires neutral decision-makers, equal opportunity to present evidence, and reasoned, consistent rulings. It is a foundational requirement for legitimate dispute-resolution and arbitration mechanisms, including those implemented on-chain."@en ;
