ngm:kernel-methods a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Kernel Methods"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Kernel methods are a class of machine learning algorithms that operate on data implicitly mapped into a high-dimensional feature space via a kernel function, without computing coordinates in that space. The kernel trick replaces inner products with kernel evaluations, enabling linear algorithms to learn non-linear relationships. They underpin support vector machines, Gaussian processes and kernel ridge regression."@en ;
