ngm:go-quorum a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GoQuorum"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "GoQuorum is an open-source, enterprise-focused Ethereum client originally developed by J.P. Morgan and forked from go-ethereum to support permissioned consortium networks. It adds private transactions and contracts, permissioning, and pluggable consensus algorithms such as IBFT, QBFT, and Raft suited to known-validator settings. It is widely used to build private and consortium blockchains for financial and supply-chain applications."@en ;
