ngm:query-strategy a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Query Strategy"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A query strategy is the policy by which an active-learning system selects which unlabelled instances to request labels for, aiming to maximise model improvement per labelling cost. Common strategies include uncertainty sampling, query-by-committee, and expected model change. It is the decision-making core that makes active learning more label-efficient than passive supervised learning."@en ;
