ngm:autonomous-mobile-robots a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Autonomous Mobile Robots"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Robotic platforms capable of self-directed locomotion through environments, navigating without fixed infrastructure guidance by using onboard sensing, mapping, localisation, and path-planning capabilities. Autonomous mobile robots (AMRs) operate in dynamic, human-shared spaces and are distinguished from automated guided vehicles (AGVs) by their ability to adapt routes in real time rather than following pre-defined paths."@en ;
