ngm:deep-reinforcement-learning a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Deep Reinforcement Learning"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) is a machine learning paradigm that combines deep neural networks with reinforcement learning, enabling agents to learn optimal policies for sequential decision-making tasks by interacting with an environment, receiving scalar reward signals, and updating neural network parameters through gradient-based optimisation. It has produced superhuman performance in games, robotics control, and language model alignment."@en ;
