    rdfs:comment "Probabilistic finality is a transaction confirmation model characteristic of longest-chain consensus mechanisms where confidence in transaction irreversibility increases exponentially with block depth, approaching but never reaching absolute certainty, with reversal probability decaying as (q/p)^..."@en ;
