    rdfs:comment "Conviction Voting is a continuous-time, conviction-weighted decentralised governance mechanism — originally formalised by Block Science researchers Jeff Emmett, Michael Zargham and Jessica Zartler in the 2019 working paper Conviction Voting: A Novel Continuous Decision Making Alternative to G..."@en ;
